Z||000031||Carrolles||10-04-1999||05:37 PM||||I bought a simple headlight reminder buzzer at K-mart for about $6.00.  It plugs into the fuse block with a couple of included fuse taps.  One lead connects to any point that is hot when the lights are on and the other plugs into a spot that is hot when the ignition is on and grounded when the ignition is off.  When the ignition switch is on, both spots are at 12v+ and therefore no current through the buzzer.  When the ignition is off, one is 12V+ and the other is grounded, therefore 12v goes through the buzzer and makes it sound.  Radio Shack has the same 12V buzzer for about $3.00 without the fuse taps. The buzzer is about 1/2" by 1" and has double sided sticky tape to attach it under the dash.<P>This is far cheaper than replacing the GM convenience module for about $40.00.<P>Take care,<BR>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000032||Patrick||10-04-1999||09:41 PM||||<BR><B>$40 ??!!!</B><P>Is this "GM convenience module" the same thing as the "chime unit" that Ogre was saying was $3 or $4 at Kmart? I was joking earlier that it probably would be $25 or so at a GM parts counter. Did I underestimate by 15 bucks?||||reg||4
Z||000033||batboy||10-04-1999||09:55 PM||||Thanks Carroll and Ogre, that's exactly what I was wanting. Next time I'm in K-Mart, I'll look for that light reminder device.||||reg||1
